WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.000
Adobe Creative Cloud is useful in eLearning as a media and asset-production ecosystem.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.035
It can support the creation of visuals, audio, video, motion, documents,

00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:13.000
branding elements, and reusable design assets that eventually become part of a course.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
It is not, by itself, a learning management system or a complete instructional strategy.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.260
It is a toolkit that helps production teams make learning materials clearer and more

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.000
polished.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
A healthy eLearning workflow separates responsibilities.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Authoring tools assemble the course experience.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.210
Media production tools create graphics, narration, video, and documents.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.944
Review workflows collect comments and approvals.

00:00:32.944 --> 00:00:35.000
SCORM packages package the course for tracking.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
LMS platforms launch the course, manage learner access,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
and report completion or score data.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.240
Confusing these roles can lead to unrealistic expectations and messy projects.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.000
Creative Cloud assets can include diagrams, icons, screen graphics, course thumbnails,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
narration audio, short videos, motion graphics, PDFs, job aids, worksheets,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.000
and visual summaries.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.930
These assets may be used inside a SCORM course, a knowledge base,

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.000
a blended learning program, or a performance-support library.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.500
The same source asset might also be exported in different formats for different delivery

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.200
needs.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.000
Instructional design should come before visual production.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.905
Before opening a design or editing tool, the team should know the learning goal, audience,

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:15.195
task context, content scope, and assessment approach.

00:01:15.195 --> 00:01:18.990
Without that plan, production can drift toward attractive but unfocused media.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:24.000
The best visuals and audio support a learning outcome;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.010
they do not compensate for a course that lacks structure.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.000
Use Creative Cloud to clarify, focus, and reinforce.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
A diagram can explain a relationship.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.000
A short video can demonstrate motion or timing.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.000
A job aid can help learners after the course is complete.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The goal is not decoration.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.780
The goal is to create assets that help learners understand, complete, apply,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.000
and revisit the material when they need it.
